{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The epoxy felt useful for small repairs alongside my fastening projects because it could bond parts where screws or nails would not suit the repair.",
    "The list partly recognized my interest in practical repair supplies, although only the epoxy felt relevant enough to choose now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My wood screws, framing nails and drywall anchors do not imply a current need for metal cutting, wiring connectors, electronics cleaner or hose fittings; those serve different tasks.",
    "The locking nuts require a bolt fastening need I have not shown, while a hose fitting would require exact matching dimensions.",
    "Twelve tubes of super glue and eighteen rolls of duct tape exceed my current needs; I would choose the epoxy for the small repairs I have in mind."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying fastening supplies seems to have been treated as interest in almost any workshop or maintenance product.",
    "My purchases of large packs of nails and screws seem to have been extended to bulk adhesives and tape, even though I need different quantities of those supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of framing nails, wood screws and drywall anchors point most clearly toward fastening wood and mounting things.",
    "Specific dimensions, fastening methods and intended materials matter more to me than a broad connection to repair work.",
    "My medicine cups and replacement vacuum bags reflect separate household needs, so I would not treat every recent purchase as part of one workshop project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but stretched them into unrelated maintenance tasks and quantities I do not currently need."
}"}
